<title>USA: Fed says it buying coupons for Tuesday delivery.</title>
<headline>Fed says it buying coupons for Tuesday delivery.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added permanent reserves to the banking system on Friday by buying coupons for delivery on Tuesday, February 18, the Fed confirmed.</p>
<p>The Fed confirmed that the coupons bore maturity dates ranging from August 31, 1997 to August 15, 1998.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-1/16 percent, below the Fed's current official target level of 5-1/4 percent, at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>(( -- E. Freilich  N.A. Treasury desk, 212-859-1663))</p>
